{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now I have a good understanding of the architecture. Let me understand the task better and what the migration needs to accomplish.\n\nThe task: KR3.3 - migrate 243 natural language subagent trigger words to explicit pi trigger syntax.\n\nKey requirements:\n1. `internal/prompt/templates/` top-level + skills/ natural language trigger words → explicit pi syntax: `workflowScript` + `runs.run`/`runs.all` + real agent names; covering sense_loop (think/research/exporter dispatch), plan (六维评审), doing/easy (Main/Sub Agent), dream, learning, ctrl\n2. Trigger ownership explicit: parent holds orchestration, single writer, async/context semantics written into relevant templates\n3. SENSE specific semantics not lost: 批判门禁, 反向回流 (回流上限), 判断记录 (judgment.md only writes human original words) remain complete in sense_loop.md after migration\n4. Verification: \n   - `grep -rcE 'workflowScript|runs\\.run|runs\\.all' internal/prompt/templates/ | grep -v ':0' | wc -l` ≥1\n   - `go build` + `go test ./internal/prompt/... -v` all green\n   - `./bin/rick plan --dry-run`/`doing --dry-run`/`human-loop --dry-run` no `{{`\n\nTest method:\n- normal path: capture baseline count of natural language trigger words first → write to `.rick/jobs/job_35/doing/trigger-baseline.txt` → migrate → grep count ≥1, and post-migration NL trigger count < baseline\n- boundary (real agent names): `grep -rcE \"agent:'worker'|agent:'reviewer'|agent:'think'|agent:'research'|agent:'exporter'\" internal/prompt/templates/ | grep -v ':0' | wc -l` ≥1\n- exception (SENSE semantics + no variable leak): `grep -cE '批判门禁|反向回流|judgment.md' internal/prompt/templates/sense_loop.md` ≥1 + `go build` + `./bin/rick plan --dry-run | grep -c '{{'` → 0; go test all green\n\nImportant constraint: The template is processed by PromptBuilder which replaces `{{variable}}`; `extractVariables` will treat any `{{...}}` as a variable. So I must NOT introduce non-variable `{{` in templates. pi's workflowScript examples use backticks/`${}` — when in Go test fixtures, handle the raw string backtick truncation issue.\n\nWait, but these are markdown templates, not Go test fixtures. The `{{` constraint is about not introducing `{{` in the .md templates (since PromptBuilder/extractVariables will treat them as variables). The `${}` in workflowScript is fine in markdown (no `{{`). So in the .md templates, I need to write `workflowScript` + `runs.run(...)` examples using JS with `${}` interpolation but WITHOUT `{{`.\n\nActually wait - I need to be careful. The pi workflowScript examples use JS template literals with `${}`. Those are fine as long as no `{{`. But I should avoid `${...}` being misinterpreted? No, `extractVariables` only looks for `{{...}}`. `${}` is fine.\n\nLet me look at the actual pi-subagents skill to understand the exact syntax I should use in the templates.\n\nLet me read the pi-subagents SKILL.md."}}
