{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now I have a full understanding of the pi subagent syntax and best practices. Let me plan the migration.\n\nKey syntax elements:\n- `subagent({ workflowScript: \"return runs.run('main', { agent: 'worker', task: '...' })\" })` — single child\n- `subagent({ workflowScript: \"const [a,b] = await runs.all([{key:'x', agent:'reviewer', task:'...'}, ...]); return ...\" })` — parallel\n- `async: true` default; `async:false` for foreground\n- `context: \"fresh\"` / `context: \"fork\"`\n- Agent names: `scout`, `worker`, `reviewer`, `researcher`, `delegate`, `oracle`/`advisor`\n- The task text = compact contract (goal/target/authority/success criteria/validation/stop rules)\n- Parent owns orchestration; ordinary children do not get subagent tool\n- one writer per cwd/worktree\n- SENSE specific: 批判门禁, 反向回流, judgment.md\n\nThe task's required agent names for the migration (per task.md and 测试方法):\n`agent:'worker'|agent:'reviewer'|agent:'think'|agent:'research'|agent:'exporter'`\n\nSo I should use these agent names. Note: think/research/exporter are custom agents (registered per KR3.2), and worker/reviewer are builtin.\n\nWait, but I need to be careful. The task says:\n> 改写为显式 pi 触发语法（`workflowScript` + `runs.run`/`runs.all` + 真实 agent 名 `agent:'worker'/'reviewer'/'think'/'research'/'exporter'`）\n\nSo the \"real agent names\" for this project are:\n- worker (builtin, single writer)\n- reviewer (builtin, review)\n- think (custom agent, from think.md)\n- research (custom agent, from research.md)\n- exporter (custom agent, from exporter.md)\n\nWait, but the pi builtin is `researcher`, not `research`. But the task explicitly says `agent:'research'`. So the rick project has registered custom agents named `think`, `research`, `exporter` (per KR3.2: \"think/research/exporter 注册为 pi 自定义 agent\"). So `research` is a custom agent name (not `researcher`). I should use the names as specified in the task: `think`, `research`, `exporter`.\n\nLet me verify what custom agents are registered. Let me check ~/.rick/pi/agent/agents/ or .pi/agents/."}}
