{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a full understanding of the pi subagent syntax and best practices. Let me plan the migration.\n\nKey syntax elements:\n- `subagent({ workflowScript: \"return runs.run('main', { agent: 'worker', task: '...' })\" })` — single child\n- `subagent({ workflowScript: \"const [a,b] = await runs.all([{key:'x', agent:'reviewer', task:'...'}, ...]); return ...\" })` — parallel\n- `async: true` default; `async:false` for foreground\n- `context: \"fresh\"` / `context: \"fork\"`\n- Agent names: `scout`, `worker`, `reviewer`, `researcher`, `delegate`, `oracle`/`advisor`\n- The task text = compact contract (goal/target/authority/success criteria/validation/stop rules)\n- Parent owns orchestration; ordinary children do not get subagent tool\n- one writer per cwd/worktree\n- SENSE specific: 批判门禁, 反向回流, judgment.md\n\nThe task's required agent names for the migration (per task.md and 测试方法):\n`agent:'worker'|agent:'reviewer'|agent:'think'|agent:'research'|agent:'exporter'`\n\nSo I should use these agent names. Note: think/research/exporter are custom agents (registered per KR3.2), and worker/reviewer are builtin.\n\nWait, but I need to be careful. The task says:\n> 改写为显式 pi 触发语法（`workflowScript` + `runs.run`/`runs.all` + 真实 agent 名 `agent:'worker'/'reviewer'/'think'/'research'/'exporter'`）\n\nSo the \"real agent names\" for this project are:\n- worker (builtin, single writer)\n- reviewer (builtin, review)\n- think (custom agent, from think.md)\n- research (custom agent, from research.md)\n- exporter (custom agent, from exporter.md)\n\nWait, but the pi builtin is `researcher`, not `research`. But the task explicitly says `agent:'research'`. So the rick project has registered custom agents named `think`, `research`, `exporter` (per KR3.2: \"think/research/exporter 注册为 pi 自定义 agent\"). So `research` is a custom agent name (not `researcher`). I should use the names as specified in the task: `think`, `research`, `exporter`.\n\nLet me verify what custom agents are registered. Let me check ~/.rick/pi/agent/agents/ or .pi/agents/.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_laP3GIxBnPNh4UfOGIks7971","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && echo \"=== ~/.rick/pi/agent/agents ===\"; ls -la ~/.rick/pi/agent/agents/ 2>&1; echo \"=== .pi/agents ===\"; ls -la .pi/agents/ 2>&1; echo \"=== find agents md ===\"; find ~/.rick/pi/agent -maxdepth 3 -name '*.md' 2>/dev/null | head -40; echo \"=== .pi dir ===\"; find .pi -type f 2>/dev/null | head -40"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_gAx48J5gkqyPMsj50fK50879","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && grep -rn 'agent' internal/env/*.go 2>/dev/null | grep -iE 'think|research|exporter|worker|reviewer|agent' | head -40; echo \"=== env dir ===\"; ls -la internal/env/ 2>/dev/null; echo \"=== find agent registration ===\"; grep -rn 'think\\|research\\|exporter' internal/ --include=*.go | grep -iE 'agent|frontmatter|agents/' | head -30"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":5791,"output":899,"cacheRead":93312,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":571,"totalTokens":100002,"cost":{"input":0.002519085,"output":0.00078213,"cacheRead":0.000338256,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0036394709999999996}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914953387,"responseId":"d53f7287-52c8-435f-bfcc-25dcdc1f33fb","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_laP3GIxBnPNh4UfOGIks7971","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== ~/.rick/pi/agent/agents ===\nls: cannot access '/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/agents/': No such file or directory\n=== .pi/agents ===\nls: cannot access '.pi/agents/': No such file or directory\n=== find agents md ===\n=== .pi dir ===\n.pi/subagents/artifacts/0c46aba6_reviewer_0_transcript.jsonl\n.pi/subagents/artifacts/c