{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"This is the acceptance test. Let me understand the exact requirements:\n\n1. Baseline capture: `python3 task11.py --dump-baseline` must be run BEFORE migration. It counts matches of TRIGGER_RE across all .md files and writes to trigger-baseline.txt.\n\n2. Test 1: pi_files (files matching `workflowScript|runs\\.run|runs\\.all`) >= 1; current trigger count < baseline.\n\n3. Test 2: agent_files (files matching `agent:'worker'|agent:'reviewer'|agent:'think'|agent:'research'|agent:'exporter'`) >= 1.\n\n4. Test 3: sense_loop.md matches `批判门禁|反向回流|judgment\\.md` >= 1; go build passes; plan --dry-run has no `{{`; go test ./internal/prompt/... passes.\n\nImportant: the trigger regex counts things like `派发 subagent`, `SPAWN Sub Agent`, `SPAWN Step`, `子 Agent`, `父 Agent`, `Main Agent`, `Sub Agent`, `每个 subagent 独立启动`.\n\nNote: The trigger regex is case-insensitive. So \"subagent\" in general is NOT counted (only `派发 subagent`, `SPAWN Sub Agent`, `SPAWN Step`, `子 Agent`, `父 Agent`, `Main Agent`, `Sub Agent`, `每个 subagent 独立启动`).\n\nSo my migration needs to reduce these specific phrases. Important: I need to be careful — when I add `workflowScript` examples with `runs.run(...)`, I might write \"Sub Agent\" or \"Main Agent\" as part of explanation. I should avoid those exact phrases (case-insensitive). Also \"子 Agent\", \"父 Agent\".\n\nActually, the key is: the baseline count needs to be > 0 (it currently is), and after migration, current < baseline.\n\nLet me first run the baseline dump, then do the migration.\n\nLet me also understand: what's the current trigger count? Let me compute it.\n\nLet me run the baseline dump now (before migration), and also check current count.\n\nActually, let me first look at all the templates and understand the full scope of natural language trigger words I need to migrate. I've read most of them. Let me now:\n\n1. Run baseline dump\n2. Do migration\n3. Run tests\n\nLet me first check the current trigger count using the regex.\n\nLet me run the baseline capture first (this is required before migration)."}}
