{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me migrate plan.md (六维评审 → reviewer agents).\n\nplan.md trigger phrase: \"每个 subagent 独立启动\" (1 match, line 118).\n\nThe 六维评审 section (lines 118-125):\n```\n7. **六维评审**（每个 subagent 独立启动，**串行执行**，上一个完成后再启动下一个）：\n   - subagent_1：一致性检查 —— ...\n   - subagent_2：loops/skills 利用检查 —— ...\n   - subagent_3：依赖关系完整性 —— ...\n   - subagent_4：执行风险推演 —— ...\n   - subagent_5：测试用例完整性 —— ...\n   - subagent_6：端到端验证设计 —— ...\n   - 每个 subagent 输出评审结论后，根据结论修正 task 文件，再启动下一个\n```\n\nI need to convert this to explicit pi syntax. The six reviews are read-only reviews (consistency, loops/skills usage, dependency completeness, execution risk, test completeness, e2e validation). These should be `reviewer` agents. But note: the six reviews are SERIAL (each one runs, then fix, then next). Under pi, this could be:\n- Serial: `runs.run` for each reviewer sequentially, OR\n- Parallel: `runs.all` with 6 reviewers (but they're read-only and the \"fix after each\" is serial).\n\nActually, the current design is serial (fix after each review). But reviews are read-only, so they COULD be parallelized (BP: \"Prefer fresh-context review/validation fanout, then synthesize and apply fixes in the parent\"). The best practice is parallel review fanout + synthesize + apply.\n\nBut to preserve the existing serial semantics (each review → fix → next), I'll keep it as a serial workflow but express it with explicit syntax. Actually, the task says \"plan（六维评审）\" — I need to cover it. Let me express it with a workflowScript that runs 6 reviewers (can be parallel `runs.all` for the review step, then parent synthesizes and applies fixes).\n\nLet me design the new 六维评审 section:\n\n```\n7. **六维评审**（用 `subagent({ workflowScript: ... })` + `runs.all` 并行派发 6 个 `agent:'reviewer'`，fresh 上下文，只读评审；评审结果返回后由你（parent）综合修正 task 文件，再进入下一步）：\n   - agent:'reviewer' #1（一致性检查）—— 任务目标与每个 task{n}.md 的任务目标对齐，确认每个 task 的交付物都能推进对应的 KR\n   - age