{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now the trigger count should be 0. Let me verify and also check the overall status.\n\nBut wait — I also need to handle the semantically-relevant files that weren't caught by the regex but are part of the task scope:\n- skills/debug_skill.md — \"review debug agent (subagent)\" \n- skills/exporter.md — \"派发 exporter\"\n- skills/sense.md — \"research subagent\"\n- doing.md — \"调度 subagent\"\n- ctrl.md — (listed in coverage)\n- exporter.md, think.md — agent prompts\n\nLet me first verify the trigger count is now 0 and run the full acceptance test to see where I stand. But before running the full test (which includes go build + go test), let me do the remaining semantic migrations.\n\nActually, let me first check: the task's KR1 says \"覆盖 sense_loop（think/research/exporter 派发）、plan（六维评审）、doing/easy（Main/Sub Agent）、dream、learning、ctrl\".\n\nLet me check what's done:\n- sense_loop ✓ (think/research/exporter explicit)\n- plan ✓ (六维评审 → reviewer)\n- doing/easy → doing_loop.md ✓ (Main/Sub Agent → parent/worker child)\n- dream ✓ (subagent_1~4 → reviewer/worker)\n- learning → learning_loop.md ✓ (父/子 Agent → parent/worker child)\n- ctrl — NOT done yet. ctrl.md has no trigger words, but I should add trigger ownership clarification.\n\nLet me check ctrl.md for any natural language subagent references. From my earlier read, ctrl.md is a monitoring agent — it reads tasks.json, raw_session_coding.log, etc. It doesn't spawn subagents. So for ctrl, the \"迁移\" is to clarify that ctrl is a single-agent read-only monitor (no orchestration). I'll add a brief note.\n\nActually, let me re-read the task KR1 more carefully: \"覆盖 sense_loop（think/research/exporter 派发）、plan（六维评审）、doing/easy（Main/Sub Agent）、dream、learning、ctrl\".\n\nSo ctrl is in the list. But ctrl has no natural language trigger words. The migration for ctrl would be to explicitly state its trigger ownership: \"ctrl 是单 agent 只读监控，不持编排权、不派发 subagent\". Let me add that to ctrl.md's 角色 or 工作约束 section.\n\nLet me also handle:\n- doing.md (top-level) — line 5 \"你是...parent 编排者。你的任务是按依赖拓扑顺序调度 subagent 执行各 task\". This says \"调度 subagent\" — not a trigger phrase, but semantically I should make it explicit. Actually, doing.md's actual workflow is injected via `{{doing_loop_content}}` (which is doing_loop.md, now migrated). The doing.md line 5 is a role definition. Let me update it to reference explicit syntax.\n\nLet me look at doing.md line 5 again:\n```\n你是一个资深的软件工程师，同时是本次 job 的 parent 编排者。你的任务是按依赖拓扑顺序调度 subagent 执行各 task，完成具体的编码工作。\n```\n\nI'll update \"调度 subagent\" → \"用 workflowScript + runs.run 调度 worker child\".\n\n- skills/debug_skill.md — \"review debug agent (subagent)\" → should reference agent:'reviewer'. Let me migrate the \"review debug agent\" to explicit reviewer.\n\n- skills/exporter.md — \"sense_loop 派发 exporter\" → already has \"派发\" but not \"派发 subagent\". Semantically, exporter is a child agent. Let me add a note.\n\n- skills/sense.md — \"research subagent 大量调研\" → these are role references in the sense methodology. Not trigger words. But for consistency, I could update. Low priority.\n\n- think.md, research.md, exporter.md (top-level) — these are the agent prompts. They describe their own roles (\"research = child agent...\" done for research; think.md says \"think = 推理过程分析师\"; exporter.md says \"接收 sense_loop 派发\"). These are fine — they're the child agent's own system prompts, describing what they ARE, not how to trigger. I'll add a brief note to think.md and exporter.md clarifying they're child agents (no subagent tool), similar to what I did for research.md.\n\nActually, let me be pragmatic. The acceptance test only requires:\n1. pi_files >= 1 ✓\n2. trigger count < 109 ✓ (now 0)\n3. agent_files >= 1 ✓\n4. sense_loop SENSE semantics ✓\n5. go build + go test + plan dry-run ✓ (need to verify)\n\nThe semantic requirements (KR1/KR2/KR3) are mostly covered. Let me do a few more high-value edits (ctrl.md note, doing.md role line, debug_skill.md reviewer) then run the full verification.\n\nLet me first do the remaining edits, then verify.\n\n### ctrl.md\nAdd a note in the 角色 or 工作约束 section clarifying ctrl is single-agent read-only (no orchestration). Let me add to 工作约束 section.\n\nCurrent ctrl.md 工作约束:\n```\n## 工作约束\n\n- **展示计划再执行**：写文件前必须向人类说明将要做什么，获得明确确认\n- **非侵入**：不终止 doing 进程，只通过文件修改影响未来行为\n- **范围限制**：只能修改 `{{doing_dir}}/` 和 `{{plan_dir}}/` 下的文件\n- **诚实**：日志不存在时如实告知（任务尚未开始执行，或首次运行）\n```\n\nI'll add:\n```\n- **无编排权**：ctrl 是单 agent 只读监控，不持 subagent 工具，不派发任何 child；不触发 workflowScript/runs.run\n```\n\n### doing.md\nLine 5: update \"调度 subagent\" → explicit.\n\n### debug_skill.md\nMigrate \"review debug agent (subagent)\" → \"agent:'reviewer'\".\n\nLet me also check debug_skill.md has a \"review debug agent 协议\" section with \"由主 Agent 启动的 subagent\". Let me update those.\n\nLet me do these edits now. First, let me read the exact text of the relevant lines.\n\nFor debug_skill.md, the relevant lines:\n- Line 71: \"在 Phase 1 建立假设时，启动 **review debug agent**（subagent）：\"\n- Line 111: \"在 Phase 3 生成假设时，启动 **review debug agent**（subagent）：\"\n- Line 223: \"review debug agent 是在调试特定触发点由主 Agent 启动的 subagent，职责是**深度分析**，不执行任何修改。\"\n\nLet me update these to reference agent:'reviewer' explicitly.\n\nFor debug_skill.md, I'll:\n1. Line 71: \"启动 **review debug agent**（subagent）\" → \"启动 **review debug agent**（`agent:'reviewer'`）\"\n2. Line 111: same\n3. Line 223: \"review debug agent 是在调试特定触发点由主 Agent 启动的 subagent\" → \"review debug agent 是在调试特定触发点由 parent 用 `runs.run` 启动的 `agent:'reviewer'`\"\n\nAlso add a trigger syntax example. Let me add it in the \"review debug agent 协议\" section.\n\nLet me also check the \"反模式\" table has \"先触发 review debug agent\" — fine.\n\nLet me now do all these remaining edits.\n\nActually, let me be careful about scope. The task is primarily about the trigger-word migration (which is now complete: 0 trigger words). The additional semantic edits (ctrl, doing role, debug_skill reviewer) are \"nice to have\" for full KR coverage. Let me do them concisely.\n\nLet me do doing.md, ctrl.md, debug_skill.md, and add brief notes to think.md and exporter.md and skills/exporter.md.\n\nLet me first do doing.md role line."}}
