{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now let me add brief notes to think.md and exporter.md (top-level agent prompts) clarifying they're child agents (no subagent tool), similar to research.md. And skills/exporter.md and skills/sense.md.\n\nActually, let me focus. think.md and exporter.md are the child agent system prompts. Let me add a one-line clarification to each.\n\nFor think.md (top-level), the role section:\n```\n# think subagent\n...\n## 角色\n\nthink = 推理过程分析师 + 风险评估师。...\n```\n\nLet me add a note at the top similar to research.md. Actually, think.md's title is \"# think subagent\". Let me change it to \"# think agent（agent:'think'）\" and add a note.\n\nWait, but think.md is loaded via LoadTemplate(\"think\") in human_loop_prompt.go and its content is written to prompts/think.md. There's a test TestThinkTemplateHasPipeline that checks for keywords. Changing the title shouldn't break it. But let me be careful.\n\nActually, let me check: does any test check think.md's title \"# think subagent\"? Let me search.\n\nActually, I already saw the tests (human_loop_prompt_test.go) — TestThinkTemplateHasPipeline checks for \"演绎\", \"归纳\", \"溯因\", etc. No title check. TestThinkTemplateDeletesExplicitAssumptionDuty checks for forbidden strings. So changing the title is safe.\n\nSimilarly exporter.md — TestExporterTemplateHasTwoPhase checks for \"大纲\", \"内容\". Safe.\n\nLet me add brief notes. For think.md:\n- Title \"# think subagent\" → \"# think agent（agent:'think'）\"\n- Add note after title: \"> 本 prompt 是 pi 自定义 agent `think` 的子任务 prompt（agent:'think'），由 sense_loop parent 用 runs.run 派发；think 不持 subagent 工具，不递归派发。\"\n\nFor exporter.md:\n- Title \"# exporter subagent\" → \"# exporter agent（agent:'exporter'）\"\n- Add similar note.\n\nFor skills/exporter.md:\n- Title \"# skill:exporter（RFC 输出方法论）\" → add note it's the agent system prompt.\n- \"与其他 subagent 的协作\" → \"与其他 agent 的协作\" (and update the \"派发 exporter\" reference).\n\nFor skills/sense.md:\n- It has \"research subagent 大量调研\" and \"think subagent 对每个候选\". These are not trigger phrases. But for consistency, I could leave them (they describe the methodology roles). Low priority — I'll leave sense.md mostly as-is since it's a methodology skill, not a trigger instruction. Actually, let me update the few \"subagent\" role references to be consistent. But it's low value. Let me skip sense.md to avoid over-editing.\n\nActually, wait — let me reconsider. The task says \"skills/ 109 处\" total trigger words, and I've reduced to 0. The remaining natural language \"subagent\" references (like \"research subagent\" in sense.md) are role DESCRIPTIONS, not trigger WORDS. The task's regex-defined trigger words are all eliminated. So I'm good on the core requirement.\n\nLet me do the think.md and exporter.md title + note updates, and skills/exporter.md, then verify.\n\nLet me do think.md first."}}
