{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Interesting:\n- `git ls-files --stage bin/rick` → shows it's tracked with hash `730a7db7...`\n- `git diff --stat bin/rick` → EMPTY (no diff!)\n\nSo `bin/rick` is tracked, and there's NO diff (the working tree binary matches the index). But earlier `git status --short bin/` showed `M  bin/rick`.\n\nWait, that's contradictory. `git diff --stat bin/rick` is empty, but `git status` showed \"M\". Let me re-run git status.\n\nOh wait — I already committed my template changes, and then ran `go build -o bin/rick`. The `go build` recreated bin/rick with the new embedded templates. But `git diff --stat bin/rick` shows empty?? That means the binary content is the same as the index?\n\nActually, that can't be right — the templates changed, so the embedded content changed, so the binary should differ.\n\nWait, let me reconsider. Maybe `git diff --stat bin/rick` returns empty because the file is binary and... no, git diff --stat would still show \"Bin ... bytes\" for binary changes.\n\nHmm, actually, maybe the `git status --short bin/` \"M bin/rick\" was from BEFORE my commit (the status was showing the OLD state). After my commit of templates, I ran `go build -o bin/rick`, which updated bin/rick. But then `git add bin/rick` failed with \"ignored\".\n\nWait, but now `git diff --stat bin/rick` is empty. That's weird.\n\nLet me re-check the current full git status.\n\nActually, I bet what happened is: \n1. Before my work, bin/rick was modified (M) due to a previous task's build.\n2. I ran `git add internal/prompt/templates/` and committed. This did NOT include bin/rick.\n3. I ran `go build -o bin/rick ./cmd/rick` — this rebuilt bin/rick with my new templates.\n4. `git add bin/rick` failed \"ignored\".\n\nBut `git diff --stat bin/rick` now empty means the working bin/rick == index bin/rick (hash 730a7db7). \n\nWait, this suggests my `go build` did NOT change bin/rick? That can't be right since I changed templates.\n\nOR — maybe the index hash `730a7db7` is from task10's rebuild, and my `go build` produced a DIFFERENT binary, but then something reset it?\n\nActually, let me just check: does the current on-disk bin/rick contain my new template content? I already verified `./bin/rick plan --dry-run` shows `agent:'reviewer'` (7 hits) and no `{{`. So the on-disk binary DOES have my new templates.\n\nBut `git diff --stat bin/rick` is empty? That means the on-disk binary matches the index. Which means the index binary ALSO has my new templates. But the index was last updated by \"chore(task10): rebuild bin/rick\"...\n\nThis is confusing. Let me just check the actual current state with a fresh git status."}}
