{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The rick-gates helper.py reports \"zombie running: task task11 仍处于 running 状态\" but EXIT=0 (odd — it printed the message but exited 0? Or the tail captured the message and the EXIT is from tail).\n\nWait, the output says \"zombie running: task task11 仍处于 running 状态\". This means tasks.json has task11 still in \"running\" state. This is expected — the rick-gates gate checks that there are no zombie running tasks. Since task11 is CURRENTLY running (I'm the task11 agent), it's \"running\". The gate will be checked AFTER my session ends, at which point the harness marks task11 as success.\n\nActually, let me understand the flow better. The rick-gates helper.py is called by the rick harness AFTER the pi session ends. At that point:\n1. The harness checks my work.\n2. The harness marks task11 as \"success\" with commit_hash in tasks.json.\n3. Then it runs helper.py to validate (no zombie running, success has commit_hash).\n\nSo the \"zombie running\" message is EXPECTED during my session (task11 is still running). The harness will handle the final state transition.\n\nBut wait — the doing_loop.md COMMIT step says the SUB AGENT (me) should run the check. But actually, looking at the flow, the rick-gates is run by the HARNESS (rick side), not by me. The prompt says:\n\n\"2. 确认门禁（rick-gates）通过：rick 侧会在 pi 会话结束后调用 `python3 .rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py <doing_dir>` 校验\"\n\n\"rick 侧会在 pi 会话结束后调用\" = \"the rick side will call it AFTER the pi session ends\". So I don't need to run it — the harness does.\n\nBut the task11_doing_prompt.md's \"第二步：格式检查\" says to run `rick tools doing_check job_35`. Since doing_check is deleted, this instruction is stale. The actual gate is rick-gates (run by harness after session).\n\nSo my responsibilities are:\n1. ✅ Do the migration (done).\n2. ✅ Commit with task ID (done).\n3. ✅ Verify tests pass (done — task11.py passes).\n4. The harness will